{"availability":"available","full":"therealarthur/myrlin-workbook","name":"myrlin-workbook","description":"Open-source workspace manager for AI coding CLIs: Claude Code and ChatGPT Codex in one browser app. Discovers every session on disk, embedded terminals, phone-ready, cost tracking, kanban, docs. Windows, macOS, Linux.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":387,"forks":50,"created":"2026-02-06T08:59:10Z","updated":"2026-09-29T19:16:45Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://therealarthur.github.io/myrlin-workbook/","topics":["agent-orchestration","ai-agents","chatgpt","claude-code","codex","coding-agents","developer-tools","multi-provider","nodejs","self-hosted","session-manager","terminal","windows","workspace-manager","xterm"],"demo":"https://therealarthur.github.io/myrlin-workbook/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T09:02:08.978Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T09:02:08.978Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T09:02:08.978Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T09:02:08.978Z","stars":387,"forks":50}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Every Claude Code and ChatGPT Codex session on your machine, in one sidebar.","I run Claude Code all day and I started running Codex alongside it. Between the two there are a few hundred conversations on this machine, spread across two CLIs that do not know about each other, in a dozen project folders, and the only way to get back to one is to pick a UUID out of a list. Open three at once and you are juggling terminal windows. Restart the machine and you reopen everything by hand. Scroll up in a pane to find what an agent did an hour ago and you hit the top of the buffer, because a coding agent repaints its screen and keeps no scrollback at all.","So I built the thing I wanted. Myrlin reads both CLIs where they already store their data, groups every session by the folder it ran in, and opens any of them in a real terminal in a browser tab. You can wheel back through the whole conversation, drag a selection across an hour of history and copy it. Costs come out of the transcripts. Docs, a kanban board and git worktrees sit next to the sessions they belong to. It runs on your phone over your own network."],"features":["Claude Code sessions are read from /.claude/projects. Codex sessions are read from /.codex, including state5.sqlite, which is the same thread store the ChatGPT desktop app lists from, so the folders and sessions you see…","xterm.js over node-pty, so it is a real PTY. On Windows that is ConPTY directly, with no WSL; macOS and Linux use their own. Wheel up past the top of what a pane has drawn and it carries on into the recorded…","Codex threads come out of the SQLite database the desktop app uses, through an in-memory byte image, so no write handle is ever opened against your session history. A filesystem walk over the rollout JSONL stays as a…","Five tabs: Home, Sessions, Terminal, Attention and Search. Attention carries the only persistent badge in the app, counting what is waiting on you. Flick up past the top of a terminal and the history opens and keeps…","Two independent choices. The app chrome is light or dark, toggled from the topbar. The terminal palette is one of thirteen: Mocha, Macchiato, Frappé, Nord, Dracula, Tokyo Night, Cherry, Ocean, Amber and Mint in the dark…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/therealarthur/myrlin-workbook/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c4ecd551bc83145d48576410c448fe9a8126864fdf56ae7e579cc84a3c7afe05","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T09:02:09.049Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T09:02:09.049Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Every Claude Code and ChatGPT Codex session on your machine, in one sidebar.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/therealarthur/myrlin-workbook/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"c4ecd551bc83145d48576410c448fe9a8126864fdf56ae7e579cc84a3c7afe05","sourceUrl":"https://github.co